uqair|Saudipedia — Historic al-Uqayr Port|https://saudipedia.com/en/historic-al-uqayr-port|Al-Ahsa historic maritime gateway for Najd; King Abdulaziz developed customs, passports and Al-Khan resting building. Indexed source text verified despite intermittent full-page timeout.
tarout|Saudipedia — Tarout Castle|https://saudipedia.com/en/tarout-castle|Castle on Tarout Island in Al-Qatif. Do not use disputed builder, date or unverified Ishtar-name etymology.
tash|Saudipedia — Tash Ma Tash Series|https://saudipedia.com/en/tash-ma-tash-series|Nasser Al-Qasabi performed iconic character Fuad. Indexed text verified; no unsupported episode or season totals.
badr|Saudipedia — Badr bin Abdulmohsen|https://saudipedia.com/en/badr-bin-abdulmohsen|Poet known as Word Engineer; wrote Fawq Ham Al-Sahab sung by Mohammed Abdu; six poetry collections include Wamd. Avoid source's mismatched Hijri/Gregorian event dates.
shubra|Saudipedia — Historic Shubra Palace|https://saudipedia.com/%D9%82%D8%B5%D8%B1-%D8%B4%D8%A8%D8%B1%D8%A7-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%AE%D9%8A|Taif palace name derives from design inspired by a palace in Cairo's Shubra district. Exclude room counts and construction-date discrepancies.
najdimosque|Saudipedia — Al Najdi Mosque|https://saudipedia.com/en/al-najdi-mosque|Farasan mosque built by pearl merchant Ibrahim Al-Najdi; decorative panels imported from India, construction by Yemeni architects. Exclude contradictory start/completion date claims.
faisalprize|King Faisal Prize — Official history|https://kingfaisalprize.org/|Established 1977 and first awarded 1979. Distinguish establishment from first award.
zewail|King Faisal Prize — Ahmed H. Zewail|https://kingfaisalprize.org/professor-ahmed-h-zewail/|1989 Science laureate honored for laser radiation and chemical-reaction control; later Nobel chemistry laureate. Ask Saudi prize identity context, not unrelated personal trivia.
wahbah|International Union of Geological Sciences — Al Wahbah maar crater|https://iugs-geoheritage.org/geoheritage_sites/the-pleistocene-al-wahbah-dry-maar-crater/|Crater formed by explosive interaction of magma and groundwater; Harrat Kishb. No meteor-impact folklore or absolute size ranking.
thajmask|Saudipedia — Mask of the Princess of Thaj|https://saudipedia.com/%D9%82%D9%86%D8%A7%D8%B9-%D8%A3%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%B1%D8%A9-%D8%AB%D8%A7%D8%AC|Gold funerary mask of young girl excavated near Thaj in Eastern Province. Royal title conventional archaeological label, not proven historical genealogy.
fuad1994|FIFA — Fuad Anwar interview on USA 1994|https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/1994usa/news/anwar-we-surprised-the-world-in-1994|First Saudi World Cup scorer Fuad Anwar against Netherlands; Jorge Solari coach; Sweden round-of-16 opponent; Sami Al Jaber penalty opened Morocco match. First-person primary interview.
okhdood|Saudipedia — Al-Okhdood Archaeological City|https://saudipedia.com/en/al-okhdood-archaeological-city|Najran city also called Raqamat/Rijmat; caravans on Incense Route. Avoid unverified ancient casualty counts and excavation dimensions.
abdulghani|Saudipedia — Hussein Abdulghani|https://saudipedia.com/en/hussein-abdulghani|Played abroad at Swiss Neuchatel Xamax before joining Al-Nassr in 2009; Ferreya in Bulgaria later. Exclude date-of-birth discrepancies.
souanearly|Saudipedia — Hadi Souan|https://saudipedia.com/%D9%87%D8%A7%D8%AF%D9%8A-%D8%B5%D9%88%D8%B9%D8%A7%D9%86|Joined Damac in Khamis Mushayt; began as football goalkeeper before coach encouraged athletics. Distinct from Sydney medal fact; do not call silver medalist Olympic champion.
mater|British Museum — Magnetism collection record|https://www.britishmuseum.org/collection/object/W_2012-6018-3|Ahmed Mater al-Ziad created Magnetism, photographing installation of magnet and iron filings; associated with Kaaba. Ask creator, not museum inventory number.
manal|Manal AlDowayan — Suspended Together|https://www.manaldowayan.com/artworks/36-suspended-together/|Artist's own 2011 installation uses dove sculptures bearing donated women's travel-permission documents. Arabic artist title Fi al-hawa sawa; historical artwork, not a claim about current law.
bookofsun|MUBI — The Sun of Gnosis film credits|https://mubi.com/en/us/films/the-sun-of-gnosis|2020 Saudi film Shams Al-Maarif directed by Faris Godus; English title also known as The Book of Sun.
ibnbishr|New York University Libraries — Unwan al-Majd primary book catalog|https://sites.dlib.nyu.edu/viewer/books/aub_aco001264/display?lang=en|Author Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Bishr; primary digitized edition of Unwan al-Majd fi Tarikh Najd.
kiswalocation|Saudi Press Agency — Saudi Kiswa craftsmanship history|https://www.spa.gov.sa/2115541|Kaaba Kiswa factory in Umm Al-Jud district, Makkah. Exclude conflicting Hijri/Gregorian renaming years.
nassiflibrary|Saudipedia — Nassif Haus|https://saudipedia.com/de/nassif-haus|Nassif House library collections donated to King Abdulaziz University after Omar Nassif's death; German indexed source independently verified, not inferred from a guessed translation.
matermedical|Ahmed Mater — Antenna official exhibition|https://www.ahmedmater.com/exhibitions/ahmed-mater-antenna|X-ray series created when Mater was practicing medicine. Historical profession, no current employment assumption.
alarab|Saudipedia — Al-Arab magazine|https://saudipedia.com/%D9%85%D8%AC%D9%84%D8%A9-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D8%B1%D8%A8|Hamad Al-Jasser founded cultural magazine Al-Arab in 1966; Arab intellectual heritage, history and literature.
aljazirafounder|Al-Jazirah — Official newspaper search-page masthead|https://search.al-jazirah.com.sa/cgi-bin/utf_search/utf_main_search.cgi|Newspaper founded by Abdullah bin Khamis; first issue monthly magazine April 1960. Distinguish Saudi newspaper from Qatar's Al Jazeera broadcaster.
hira|Ministry of Hajj and Umrah — Hira Cave official guide|https://media1.haj.gov.sa/storage/uploads/EN-108.pdf|Hira Cave north of Grand Mosque at top of Jabal Al-Nour. Primary ministry guide, independently corroborated by Saudipedia Jabal Al-Nour article.
